  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya bilateral programme - green, sustainable and inclusive growth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Micro Enterprises Support Programme Trust: Greening the value chains

World Bank: Financing Locally-Led Climate Action program: Delivering locally-led climate resilience actions and strengthening county and national governments&apos; capacity to manage climate risks

Trade Mark East Africa: Improving business competitiveness through reduced barriers to trade and increased market access

Kenya Climate Investment Centre: Enhanced commercialization and scale-up of climate solutions/green businesses contributing to local climate mitigation and adaptation</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective of the Project is to promote green, sustainable and inclusive economic growth and decent jobs with an emphasis on youth and investors with relevant solutions (SDG 7, SDG 8, SDG 12, SDG 13).

The Partners for the Project are Micro  Enterprise Support Programme Trust (MESPT) who will focus on greening value chains; World Bank who is working with Environmental/climate governance in Kenya; Trade Mark Africa (TMA) who will be working on green regional Trade and Kenya Climate Innovations Centre (KCIC) who will be supporting on climate technologies and related innovative business models.</narrative>
  </description>
